artifact.self_contained_problem:
Let $M$ denote either the closed annulus $\mathbb{T}^1 \times [-1,1]$ (where $\mathbb{T}^1 = \mathbb{R}/\mathbb{Z}$) or the 2-sphere $S^2$, equipped with the standard Lebesgue (area) measure. Does there exist a real-analytic ($C^\omega$) diffeomorphism $f: M \to M$ such that:
(i) $f$ is homotopic to the identity;
(ii) $f$ preserves the Lebesgue measure;
(iii) $f$ has only finitely many periodic orbits; and
(iv) $f$ has a dense orbit (i.e., there exists $x \in M$ whose forward orbit $\{f^n(x): n \geq 0\}$ is dense in $M$)?

